  "description": "A supertanker (according to analysts, GEM No. 2) was struck on 09.10.2026; from 19.10 it leaked oil about 25 km off Umm Al Quwain, on 22.10 oil reached the shore, on 30.10 the leak was stopped. The exact position of the tanker was not published. During the leak the sea was almost calm (~2–3 m/s), so on L-band the slick is hard to tell from calm water. Slicks are outlined automatically from NISAR L-band images (HH); the 'oil-likeness' score is a ranking for review, not proof. Dates before 09.10 are controls without the leak.",
